data.content:
**Yes, C# fully supports `stackalloc`'d `Span<nint>` and `Span<nuint>`.** Both work without requiring `unsafe` — you can write:

```csharp
Span<nint>  nints  = stackalloc nint[5];
Span<nuint> nuints = stackalloc nuint[3];
```

This has been supported since C# 9 / .NET 5 (when `nint`/`nuint` were introduced). The only caveat is that `sizeof(nint)` requires an `unsafe` context since the size isn't fixed at compile time — use `nint.Size` instead if you need it in safe code.
